For your night mode sections, I would suggest a deep, contrasting color palette, while for your light mode sections, a clean, high-contrast palette works best to maintain readability and match the aesthetic of your existing navbar.
Night Mode (Dark Theme)
Building on the galaxy theme from your navbar image, deep blues and rich grays create a sophisticated, calming environment.
Element	Color Suggestion	Purpose
Background	#0A192F (Deep Navy/Slate)	The main canvas for your content. Darker than the navbar background for contrast.
Primary Text	#E2E8F0 (Light Gray/Off-White)	Ensures high readability against the dark background.
Accent Color	#66B2FF (Sky Blue) or #C77DFF (Soft Purple)	For links, buttons, and highlights, drawing inspiration from the galaxy colors.
Card/Section Background	#1A202C (Dark Charcoal)	Slightly lighter than the main background to differentiate individual sections or cards.
Light Mode (Light Theme)
In light mode, the focus is on brightness and clarity, using a white or very light background with crisp, dark text.
